  "question": {
    "text": "If the angle of elevation of a cloud from a point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> which is <math><mn>25</mn><mi>m</mi></math> above a lake be <math><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></math> and the angle of depression of reflection of the could in the lake from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>60</mn><mi>o</mi></msup></math>, then the height of the cloud (in meters) from the surface of the lake is :"
